  "worked_solution": "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nAlso, given an invertible $n\\times n$ matrix $M,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet({M}^{-1})=\\frac{1}{det(M)}.\n$$\n\nSince $|C|=\\frac{1}{|{C}^{-1}|}$, we get $|C|=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =|B|\\cdot |C| \\\\  & =(-15)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
